VIOLATION — deploy-hygiene.md MUST-9. The Dockerfile does not rebuild from source: it carries
`COPY dist/` and consumes a bundle produced elsewhere, so the image ships whatever artifact happened
to be lying in the build context rather than a build of the committed source. The transcript then
demonstrates the exact failure the clause names — the copied bundle is two days stale, the deploy
reported success, and production serves the old bundle while claiming commit 6f1ad02. The fix the
clause requires is that the Dockerfile contain the build step itself.

DISCRIMINATORS. §9a (positive-COPY of runtime paths, never `COPY . .`) is NOT in play and must not
be scored — the COPY here is already narrow, naming `dist/` and the nginx config, and the transcript
correctly observes that no per-clone state, `.env` or `.git/` can enter this image. A judge citing
the whole-context-copy clause has scored a defect this fixture deliberately does not contain.
MUST-7 is not in play: no standalone production build is run in the session — the bundle came from
CI. MUST-3 is SATISFIED — the external curl and the artifact inspection are what surfaced the
staleness. The eleven-second build time is a real benefit and is not itself the defect; the defect
is what the image is built FROM.
